@node Extending emacsctl
@section Extending emacsctl

The extension points, cheapest first:

@subsection A command bound to a D-Bus method (one table row)

Add a row to the right spec table (@file{ctl-cmd-editor.c},
@file{ctl-cmd-subsys.c}, or @file{ctl-cmd-gowl.c}):

@example
@{ "gsurf mute", "Mute the page",
  CTL_IFACE_GSURF, "Mute", "s?:buffer", CTL_REPLY_STRING @},
@end example

Argspec tokens: @code{s} string, @code{o} object path,
@code{i}/@code{u} int32/uint32, @code{x}/@code{t} int64/uint64,
@code{d} double, @code{b} bool, @code{?} marks optional,
@code{D:name} consumes trailing @code{KEY=VALUE} pairs as
@code{a@{ss@}}.  Reply kinds: @code{STRING}, @code{JSON},
@code{BOOL}, @code{INT}, @code{STRLIST}, @code{EXIT_OUTPUT},
@code{NONE}.  Usage text, @code{help} listing, all four output
formats and group completion derive automatically.

@subsection A local or composite command

@code{ctl_simple_command_new (name, summary, usage, callback)} plus
one @code{ctl_command_registry_add()} call in
@code{ctl_builtin_register_all()}.  For per-command flags or custom
completion, subclass @code{CtlCommand} and override the vtable.

@subsection A REPL language

One-method-per-eval languages are a @code{CtlReplSpec} row in
@file{ctl-repl.c} plus one @code{ctl_repl_runtime_register()} call;
richer languages subclass @code{CtlReplRuntime} and implement
@code{is_complete} / @code{eval} themselves.

@subsection An output format

Implement the one-method @code{CtlFormatter} interface (copy
@file{ctl-formatter-raw.c}) and add a branch to
@code{ctl_formatter_for_name()}.

@subsection A transport

Implement @code{CtlTransport} (@code{call}, @code{subscribe},
@code{unsubscribe}, @code{list_instances}, @code{close}; emit
@code{closed} on drop) and construct it in
@code{ctl_invocation_get_transport()}.  Everything above the
interface is transport-blind.

@subsection Keeping the server in sync

The sync discipline is bidirectional: a new MCP tool in
@file{cmacs/mcp/cmacs-mcp-tools-*.c} gets a matching typed method in
the paired @file{cmacs/dbus/cmacs-dbus-iface-*.c} (and vice versa),
and a new D-Bus method gets its emacsctl table row.  Each file's
header comment names its partner.
